WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.410
There was a woman who was dragged out of a town hall meeting in West Virginia

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:11.880
Simply for listing the corporate donors of politicians. I've jokingly but not I mean I guess I'm not really joking when I say it

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:16.079
politicians should display their corporate donors sort of like

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:21.270
NASCAR drivers do either on the front of their lecterns when they speak or in some other way

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:28.559
So that we know who's funding them, right, who has donated money to these politicians and Lisa Lucas went to the West

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.929
Virginia State House to testify against the bill

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:35.160
sponsored by the oil and gas industry called HB

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:42.180
4268 and it would let fossil fuel companies drill on the land of small

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.329
mineral owners without their consent and

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:48.569
What when I saw this I thought wait wait a second

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:55.379
I thought right-wingers were all about the sovereignty of land ownership and land owners

00:00:55.379 --> 00:00:57.538
But they want a bill that would let

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:04.949
Corporations use the resources of that private land without consent? Doesn't really make sense part of that double standard from the right

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.869
But that's not the story here the story is that Lisa Lucas showed up, and she said hey listen um

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.439
the people who want this garbage bill

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.669
Got money from the companies that will profit from it

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:23.640
And she started reading who got the money from these oil companies and gas companies

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:30.659
And she was told to stop and eventually she was physically removed from the room. Check this out take a listen

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:37.079
I'd also like to point out that the people who are going to be speaking in favor of this bill are all going to be

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:39.299
paid by the industry and people who are going to be

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:45.839
voting on this bill are also often paid by the industry. For example, and I have to keep it short

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:48.989
simply because the public only gets a minute forty-five

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.529
while lobbyists can throw a gala at the Marriott

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:57.869
with whiskey and wine and talk for hours to the delegates so to keep it short

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.659
on the Judiciary Committee, Charlotte Lane

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.370
about

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:10.889
$10,000 from gas and oil interest including a AEP, Marathon, First Energy Dominion, EQT, and I could go on.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.649
Next, let's talk about John Shott from Mercer: First Energy $2,000,

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:22.709
Appalachian Power $2,000, Steptoe and Johnson (that's a gas and oil law firm) $2,000,

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.590
Console Energy 1,000,

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.799
EQT 1,000, and I could go on.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.980
Now let's talk about Jason Harshbarger-- 
Miss Lucas we asked no personal comments

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.190
be made if you don't talk about--These are not personal comments-- It is a personal comment

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.999
and I'm going to call you out of order if you're talking about individuals on the committee. So

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:47.399
If you would just address the bill, if not you know I asked you to please step down.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:55.169
Jason Harshbarger took $3,500 out-- Remove--

00:02:55.169 --> 00:02:57.169
40% of his money comes from gas and oil

00:02:57.169 --> 00:02:59.169
including Dominion, EQT,

00:02:59.169 --> 00:03:01.169
First Energy, --

00:03:01.169 --> 00:03:03.169
(inaudible)

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.100
I'm not finished.-- Right.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.100
Drag me off then.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.100
People deserve someone who is going to fight for people and not corporations.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:33.639
The next speaker would be Julie Archer-- Right so you heard the phrase personal comments right they said listen

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.210
You're allowed to talk about the bill, but not about specific people involved with the bill

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:42.850
This is a totally arbitrary way to try to suppress this type of information right I mean any reasonable person

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.769
Understands if you're involved with the bill you're a big part of the bill

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:54.309
But because that's considered personal she gets dragged off here. I actually think this is a great strategy for

00:03:54.890 --> 00:04:01.210
political activism it can be really hard to show up at public comment periods at the local and state level and

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.310
Really make an impact if you show up

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:09.100
And you just start arguing about the politics of a bill you're probably not going to change a lot of minds

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.880
What about the idea of?

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.939
Showing up and doing exactly what?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:18.429
Lisa Lucas did which is you come prepared with a list of who received money from whom and you say I want to tell you

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:24.850
That this is the amount of money that these people got from one side of this and that actually could could

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.390
Transcend party lines and appeal to everybody

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:36.010
Who is sort of against the crony capitalist system of political financing that we have make it about the money?

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:40.989
Because they don't want you to know that it's about the money put it front and center

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.570
And good for Lisa here, and by the way

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:49.600
She is running for in the Democratic primary in West Virginia 7th district

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:54.040
you can look her up, it's Lisa Lucas Lisa with two S's and

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:00.490
You know the the bad news is that the bill that Lisa was testifying against did make it out of committee

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.430
It's expected to pass both the House and Senate

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:08.919
And it's eventually expected to be signed into law by the governor Republican Jim Justice

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:11.319
And it's going to be disastrous for the environment

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:15.369
But congratulations to Lisa for doing something good there should be more of this

